// tools/packs/shiloh.mjs: the curated source of the Shiloh battle pack (assets/packs/shiloh.json is generated from
// this by `node tools/build-packs.mjs shiloh`; never edit the JSON by hand).
//
// Provenance words (AGENTS.md section 3): Verified = two independent sources agree; Inferred = one source;
// Disputed = sources disagree (both given); Estimated = arithmetic or a game value, method shown.
// Research packets (2026-10-11 session): per-phase order of battle, times and events (SH1..SH4), gap-fill strengths,
// guns and arms (SH1..SH4 fill), and landmark coordinates (OSM/NPS/Wikipedia points). Their citations are carried
// on each formation below; numbers are copied from the gap-fill files unless a comment says otherwise.
//
// Positions: { lat, lon } or { near: landmark, bearing: compass degrees (0 = north, 90 = east), m: metres }, or
// { mid: [landmark, landmark] } (optionally offset the same way), or { onStream: terrain stream name, frac }.
// `bearing` on a unit is the compass direction its line faces. Every unit position is Inferred: the sources place
// units relative to fields, roads and camps (no surveyed frontages), and the 1862 field edges are not the modern
// mowed clearings. Opening positions are where each formation stood or formed at the phase's start; the player
// redeploys freely.
//
// Game choices (not history): clockRatio, men per figure (computed by build-packs), xp tiers, battery crews of 20
// per gun, AI roles, reinforcement entry points (a brigade that came into this sector at a sourced time enters
// within reach of its historical attack), objective circles and the oval shapes of the field clearings.

// ---- sources --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
